\pard\sa200\sl276\slmult1\b\f0\fs32 Obylon Sentinel MSI Deployment Guide\b0\fs22\par
\par
\b 1. System Requirements & Security Posture\b0\par
Because the Obylon Sentinel Agent leverages low-level OS hooks (Win32 API) for monitoring and enforcement, most EDRs and Anti-Virus solutions (including Windows Defender) will initially flag the installation as a false positive. This is expected behavior for this class of software and does not indicate a problem with the build.\par
\par
\b PRE-DEPLOYMENT ACTION:\b0 Before proceeding, your IT Administrator MUST add the following paths to the AV exclusion list across your fleet:\par
 - C:\\Program Files\\Obylon\\Sentinel\\*\par
 - C:\\ProgramData\\Obylon\\*\par
\par
Failure to do so will result in the AV quarantining obylon.exe and rendering the monitoring dead.\par
\par
\b VERIFYING THIS IS THE REAL BUILD:\b0 Before excluding anything from your AV, confirm what you're excluding.\par
 - This release is code-signed. Right-click obylon.exe, choose Properties, then the Digital Signatures tab, and confirm the signer is [Your Company / Publisher Name]. An unsigned obylon.exe is a reason to stop and contact us, not a reason to proceed.\par
 - The published SHA-256 checksum for this release is listed on your download page / release notes. The installer verifies this automatically during setup and will fail the install rather than run a file that doesn't match \emdash if setup fails on the download step, do not manually retry with AV disabled; contact support instead.\par
\par
\b IF YOUR ANTI-VIRUS OR EDR IS CENTRALLY MANAGED:\b0 many districts run Microsoft Defender for Business, Sophos Central, or similar tools where a single technician cannot add an exclusion locally, or where Tamper Protection blocks local changes entirely. A local exclusion attempt may appear to work but get silently overwritten by policy shortly after. If that describes your environment, this request needs to go to your district's security/network team \emdash see the accompanying \i IT Escalation Kit\i0 for a ready-to-forward request and centrally-deployable exclusion policies (Intune, GPO, and a PowerShell one-liner) so this can be pushed fleet-wide instead of machine-by-machine.\par
\par
\b IF DEFENDER STILL FLAGS A SIGNED, VERIFIED BUILD:\b0 please also report it to Microsoft so their models learn it's clean for every other Defender-protected machine, not just yours: https://www.microsoft.com/wdsi/filesubmission. Send us a copy of your submission ID and we'll follow up on our end as the publisher.\par
\par
\b 2. Zero-Touch Fleet Provisioning (Master Image Seed)\b0\par
If you select "Fleet Image" during this install, or deploy silently, you can use the Fleet Seed mode.\par
 1. Drop your enterprise license key into this exact file: C:\\ProgramData\\Obylon\\license_seed.txt\par
 2. Do this BEFORE booting the agent.\par
 3. When the agent starts, it will detect the seed file, securely provision a unique hardware UUID against the backend, and delete the seed file.\par
\par
\b CAUTION:\b0 DO NOT activate the agent and THEN capture a master Windows image for cloning! You MUST clone the image with the raw license_seed.txt file in place, not an activated vault. Otherwise, the backend will instantly reject the duplicate endpoints. Run \i obylon prep-for-image\i0 before sysprep/capture to confirm the machine is in the correct un-activated seed state.\par
\par
\b 3. The obylon Management CLI\b0\par
This MSI automatically registers C:\\Program Files\\Obylon\\Sentinel\\ to the global Windows PATH. You can open an elevated Command Prompt or PowerShell and manage the agent using the 'obylon' command.\par
\par
Available Commands:\par
 - obylon activate OBY-XXXX-XXXX-XXXX\par
 - obylon status\par
 - obylon diagnose --dev\par
 - obylon deactivate\par
 - obylon support-bundle\par
\par
By clicking "I accept the terms in the License Agreement", you acknowledge that you have read and understood these deployment requirements.\par
